#: kcmaccess.cpp:52
msgid "Audible bell"
msgstr "Chuo^ng nghe ddu+o+.c"

#: kcmaccess.cpp:58
msgid "Use &System bell"
msgstr "Du`ng chuo^ng &he^. tho^'ng"

#: kcmaccess.cpp:60
msgid "Use &customized bell"
msgstr "Du`ng chuo^ng &tu+. cho.n"

#: kcmaccess.cpp:62
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, the default system bell will be used. See the "
"\"System Bell\" control module for how to customize the system bell. "
"Normally, this is just a \"beeep\"."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u ba.n cho.n tuy` cho.n na`y, chuo^ng he^. tho^'ng ma(.c ddi.nh se~ ddu+o+c. su+? du.ng."
"Xem mo^-ddun ddie^`u khie^?n \"Chuo^ng he^. tho^'ng\" dde^? bie^'t ca'ch tuy` bie^'n"
"chuo^ng he^. tho^'ng."
"Tho^ng thu+o+`ng, no' chi? la` tie^'ng \"beeeeeeep\""

#: kcmaccess.cpp:65
msgid ""
"Check this option if you want to use a customized bell, playing a sound "
"file. If you do this, you will probably want to turn off the system bell.<p> "
"Please note that on slow machines this may cause a \"lag\" between the event "
"causing the bell and the sound being played."
msgstr ""
"Cho.n tuy` cho.n na`y ne^'u ba.n muo^'n du`ng chuo^ng tuy` bie^'n, cho+i file a^m thanh."
"Ne^'u ba.n cho.n va^.y, ba.n se~ co' the^? ta('t chuo^ng he^. tho^'ng.<p>"
"Xin luu+ y' la` vo+'i ca'c ma'y cu~ ddie^`u na`y se~ ga^y ra su+. tre^~ giu+~a"
"ca'c hie^.nt tu+o+.ng va` la`m cho chuo^ng + sound bi. cho+i."

#: kcmaccess.cpp:72
msgid "Sound to play:"
msgstr "A^m thanh se~ ddu+o+.c cho+i:"

#: kcmaccess.cpp:75
msgid "&Browse..."
msgstr "&Duye^.t..."

#: kcmaccess.cpp:77
msgid ""
"If the option \"Use customized bell\" is enabled, you can choose a sound "
"file here. Click \"Browse ...\" to choose a sound file using the file dialog."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u tuy` cho.n \"Du`ng chuo^ng tuy` bie^'n\" ddu+o+.c du`ng, ba.n se~ co' the^? cho.n"
"file a^m thanh o+? dda^y. Nha^'n \"Duye^.t\" dde^? cho.n file a^m thanh ba('ng ca'ch du`ng"
"ho^.p thoa.i."

#: kcmaccess.cpp:94
msgid "Visible bell"
msgstr "Chuo^ng nhi`n tha^'y"

#: kcmaccess.cpp:100
msgid "&Use visible bell"
msgstr "&Du`ng chuo^ng nhi`n tha^'y"

#: kcmaccess.cpp:102
msgid ""
"This option will turn on the \"visible bell\", i.e. a visible notification "
"shown every time that normally just a bell would occur. This is especially "
"useful for deaf people."
msgstr ""
"Ne^'u tuy` cho.n na`y  ba^.t \"Chuo^ng nghe ddu+o+.c\" le^n, nghi~a la` ca?nh ca'o kha? thi."
"ddu+o+c. hie^?n thi. mo^~i la^`n ma` bi`nh thu+o+`ng chi? co' chuo^ng xa?y ra."
"DDie^`u na`y thu+.c su+. hu~u+ du.ng cho nhu+~ng ngu+o+`i kho' nghe ."

#: kcmaccess.cpp:108
msgid "&Invert screen"
msgstr "DDa?&o ma`n hi`nh"

#: kcmaccess.cpp:111
msgid "All screen colors will be inverted for the amount of time specified below."
msgstr ""
"Mo.i ma`u cu?a ma`n hi`nh se~ bi. dda?o trong mo^.t khoa?ng tho+`i gian nha^'t ddi.nh"
"ddu+o+.c chi? ddi.nh du+o+'i dda^y ."

#: kcmaccess.cpp:113
msgid "&Flash screen"
msgstr "Ma`n hi`nh &cho+'p"

#: kcmaccess.cpp:115
msgid ""
"The screen will turn to a custom color for the amount of time specified "
"below."
msgstr ""
"Ma`n hi`nh se~ bi. chuye^?n tha`nh ma`u tuy` y' trong mo^.t khoa?ng tho+`i gian"
"nha^'t  ddi.nh ddu+o+c. chi? ddi.nh o+? du+o+'i dda^y . "

#: kcmaccess.cpp:121
msgid "Click here to choose the color used for the \"flash screen\" visible bell."
msgstr ""
"Nha^'n va`o dda^y dde^? cho.n ma`u se~ ddu+o+.c du`ng trong "
"chuo^ng nhi`n tha^'y cu?a \"Ma`n hi`nh cho+'p\""

